 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "The docstring of `ofComapDomain` says `comap` is its case for the rows of a cocycle, yet `comap` is defined independently. `differential_row` (Basic.lean:1039) supplies `htw` directly, and `m.mem_graded (e x) (e y)` supplies `hgr`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Homology/DG/Twisted/RowFinite/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Define `comap m e he hsupp := ofComapDomain m.m e he hsupp (fun x y \u21a6 m.mem_graded (e x) (e y)) (fun x \u21a6 m.differential_row (e x))`, then derive or drop the duplicated lemmas. The only consumer (Induction.lean:614) has `[GradedAlgebra \ud835\udc9c]`, so the `omit` gains nothing.",
   "issue": "`comap` builds the same `comapDomain e (m.m (e x))` rows as `ofComapDomain` but proves twisting a second time, with a `sum_mapDomain_index` rewrite closed by an unfolding-heavy `simpa [Finsupp.sum_apply, Finsupp.comapDomain_apply]`. `comap_m`, `comap_m_apply`, `mapDomain_comap_m` and `rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_mapDomain_comap` repeat the four `ofComapDomain` lemmas word for word.",
   "line": 657
  }
 ],
